From 360b72c751680a2be9bb6364bc9c342404a0de75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 07:09:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09277/11362] Clear the artifact-freshness backlog, and record
 a correction owed

Fourteen registered artifacts were stale against code that had drifted since they
were built. Each was resolved individually rather than acknowledged in bulk,
because a blanket acknowledgement would silence the guard instead of answering it.

REBUILT, NUMBERS UNCHANGED (7). early_stop_grace_sweep, max_actions_answer,
gateway_accurate_rescore, exp6011/6012/6013, exp6021. The three exp60xx rebuilds
are the strongest evidence available here: they EXECUTE the drifted
arc_executable_world_model.py and arc_competition_agent.py, engine guard active,
and reproduce every gate number. Verified independently before this commit --
exp6012 is 33/33 rows identical with elapsed_s the only differing field.

VERIFIED INERT, acknowledged with hash and reason (6). Acknowledgements use the
existing per-dependency mechanism, which pins the exact dependency hash and stops
applying the moment that file changes again. Two of these deliberately were NOT
rebuilt: their rebuild commands RE-MEASURE against the offline arcade, so running
them would record today's configuration rather than rebuild the July record. The
acknowledgement text says so.

CORRECTION OWED, NOT APPLIED (1). Rebuilding arc_gateway_card_ground_truth_20260727
moves published numbers: median optimism 0.018097 -> 0.02481, model-wrong 17 -> 19
of 44 cells, sign-flip membership changes, and the artifact's own gate_4
("re-run reproduces persisted trajectories") fails on 28 of 48 cells. Deterministic
across two independent rebuilds.

Attribution was probed rather than assumed. It is NOT the recent incremental
estimator: a controlled A/B on sp80@20260724@b2000 gives identical results
(1624 actions, 41 resets) at 7396dd46, HEAD~1 and HEAD, so that change's
bit-identical claim holds. The cause is live-default promotion inside the already
acknowledged window, chiefly early_stop_grace=1300 wired 2026-08-08, which
truncates b2000 cells at ~1300-1700 actions against ~1950 before.

The committed artifact is left as the July record per never-prune, with the
correction recorded in its acknowledgement text. Whether to commission a NEW
ground-truth card under current defaults is an operator decision; the producing
script's own note says a correction is a new artifact, not an overwrite.

WHAT THIS ALSO CORRECTS ABOUT YESTERDAY'S BYPASS. The previous commit used
--no-verify on the stated grounds that this lint "already fails on clean HEAD".
That was wrong. Since c6d158caea the lint separates inherited backlog, which it
downgrades, from drift the current change introduces, which it blocks. What
blocked that commit was its own new drift in scripts/arc_leaderboard_eval.py, and
the acknowledgement path was available without bypassing. The bypass converted
that new drift into inherited backlog for everyone after it. Recorded because the
mistake is easy to repeat and the gate was working correctly.

That drift is now acknowledged properly: the diff is +42/-6 confined to main()'s
write tail, after every measured value is final, and two rebuilds underneath it
reproduced their numbers exactly.

TWO DEFECTS FOUND, worth separate work. Rebuilds silently drop hand-added
top-level note fields because the preservation helper keeps only acknowledgements
-- a never-prune violation by machine, worked around by restoring the fields by
hand here. And arc_gateway_card_ground_truth.py's --rows-out defaults to a TRACKED
evidence file, which a rebuild clobbers; restored byte-identically. Same
write-target hazard class as the eval script fixed earlier today.

Lint now reports all 16 registered artifacts fresh, exit 0, hook coverage clean.
