+  "reproduces_baseline_rate_method": "CORRECTED 2026-07-27 (adversarial review). This field was previously computed as point-estimate EQUALITY (`off_rate == baseline_rate`) and published 'false' -- a non-reproduction the data never supported. It is now an interval test: 'reproduces' means the two rates are NOT DISTINGUISHABLE at the 5% level by Fisher's exact two-sided test. The winner SET genuinely does differ (reproduces_baseline_winner_set_exactly stays false, correctly, and the agent-code drift that causes it is established by serialcheck.json) -- but differing in WHICH variants win is a different claim from differing in the RATE, and only the first is supported.",
